ed}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436249 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113615" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436249 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,C=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $C$ are given above. Find $[x]_{B}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d0458bf-0ded-5bc5-82a5-015d07a4533d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436249 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose columns are the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{C} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436250 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436250 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4de2c56b-39c0-5e14-a7fb-e708db903e6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436250 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186386696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436251 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436251 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4f40a8b0-4293-52f4-8c95-85c75998d506" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436251 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436252 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436252 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "77dfbfe9-ef7f-5713-be40-7bce1749b9a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436252 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186247379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436253 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436253 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2ad54ea-289c-5268-9e48-3009985055d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436253 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186323807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436254 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f5e3b29d-0add-527d-a99b-25156b6317ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436254 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436249 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
